DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The pptthhrreeaadd__aattttrr__sseettsscchheeddppaarraamm() function sets the scheduling parameter
       attributes  of  the thread attributes object referred to by _a_t_t_r to the
       values specified in the buffer pointed to by _p_a_r_a_m.   These  attributes
       determine  the  scheduling  parameters  of  a  thread created using the
       thread attributes object _a_t_t_r.

       The pptthhrreeaadd__aattttrr__ggeettsscchheeddppaarraamm() returns the scheduling  parameter  at‐
       tributes  of the thread attributes object _a_t_t_r in the buffer pointed to
       by _p_a_r_a_m.

       Scheduling parameters are maintained in the following structure:

           struct sched_param {
               int sched_priority;     /* Scheduling priority */
           };

       As can be seen, only one scheduling parameter is  supported.   For  de‐
       tails  of the permitted ranges for scheduling priorities in each sched‐
       uling policy, see sscchheedd(7).

